<Base title="About Us" description="Disha is a voluntary organisation of IISER Pune students working for a social cause, founded in 2010.">
  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About Us</h1>
      <p>Thinking beyond self — working at the grassroots since 2010.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container container--narrow section">
    <article class="prose">
      <p>
        Disha is a voluntary organisation of IISER Pune students working for a social cause. The
        primary goal of Disha is to promote <strong>“thinking beyond self”</strong> among the entire
        student community through actually working at the grassroots for bringing about change in
        the society. The work so far has provided a very different perspective to a lot of us and
        inspired us to be <strong>active contributors, and not passive observers (or critics)</strong>
        in this process.
      </p>
      <p>
        Disha aims at generating trigger points for its volunteers — through work — to inspire and
        create leaders who will have the courage to take up the real challenges of the society on
        their shoulders, work hard to find the real solutions, and bring their dreams to reality.
      </p>
      <h2>How it started</h2>
      <p>
        Disha started informally around 2010, when a few IISER students began teaching kids from
        Someshwarwadi, a settlement near the IISER campus. It has since attained an organisational
        structure within IISER. Working in slums and villages near Pune, all Disha activities are
        primarily aimed at children, with <em>education</em> — not just conventional school education
        but in a broader sense — at the centre.
      </p>
      <p>
        The regular activities include helping kids with the school curriculum, teaching in
        innovative ways using hands-on activities and games, and conducting projects involving new
        skills and self-employment generating activities. Each place where Disha works has different
        objectives and activities planned accordingly, based on the situation there. These
        activities are coordinated and conducted entirely by the students of IISER Pune, who form
        the team of Disha.
      </p>
      <h2>Where we want to go</h2>
      <p>
        Disha aims to build a strong, robust and sustainable network of such groups across the
        youth, who would like to use their energy and intellect to effectively respond to various
        social challenges and bring about change. We believe that every youth has the fire in them
        to do good for the society, nation, world and essentially everyone. This is an appeal to
        that fire — the purest part of a human being — within every one of us, to be a part of this
        process!
      </p>
      <p>
        The detailed constitution of Disha can be found <a href="/uploads/2013/04/disha_constitution.pdf">here</a>,
        and you can meet the people running Disha on the <a href="/team">Team page</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
